Subject: [PATCH 36/36] Port the remaining Termux fixes to JDK 27

Three hunks of the Termux openjdk-25 patch series do not apply to the
JDK 27 sources because the code moved:

- os::jvm_path() moved from os_linux.cpp to os_posix.cpp, so the
  /proc/self/maps lookup that finds libjvm.so on Android has to follow.
- The --disable-new-dtags handling moved from make/autoconf/flags-cflags.m4
  to make/common/JdkNativeCompilation.gmk.

The last hunk of the Termux patch 0015 (the #endif that closes the
__ANDROID__ branch) is dropped, it was applied with a fuzz to a place
where it does not belong.

The arm-32 only part of the series (make/autoconf/flags-cflags.m4) and the
bionic statx type fix are not needed, the JDK 27 sources do not have the
problem they solve.
